# Derived reports, not publication.
#
# `python -X utf8 tools/wiki_drift.py --wiki-root repowiki report` rewrites these two
# files on every run, so tracking them meant the documented command left ` M
# repowiki/drift/DRIFT.md` + ` M repowiki/drift/drift.json` in `git status` forever, and
# whatever was committed stated a HEAD and a water level that were already stale (the
# final review measured `uncovered 888` committed against `1379` live). They are output,
# regenerable in one command from the tree they describe.
#
# The fact source stays "the Markdown here + `ledger.jsonl`". The rule lives in this
# file rather than the repository root's .gitignore because that file belongs to
# upstream and this fork's constraint is to leave it byte-for-byte alone — a deeper
# .gitignore wins for its own subtree, exactly like the .gitattributes next to it.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash on purpose. A bare `drift/` matches at any depth, so a
# page directory that happens to be named `drift/` (a strategy note on drift regimes,
# say) would vanish from `git status` without a word — the failure mode this whole
# subtree is documented for.
/drift/
